      "role": "user",
      "content": "wait so you're actually calling them goblins in your code? lol. i mean i get the metaphor, but it's a weird way to put it. \n\nit just feels like such a chaotic way to design something. if i'm trying to debug a system and i see these weird, random strings appearing everywhere, i'm gonna think there's a bug or some kind of malicious interference. how do developers actually deal with the \"mess\" without losing their minds? like, how do you distinguish between actual malicious \"noise\" and the intentional salt/junk?",
